{
	title: 'Render delayed command output as tool results',
	spec: 'In web and terminal, background Bash completions use their invocation tool colors rather than message colors. Show the actual stored command, never an invented description or Finished label; when the invocation is not loaded, identify Bash output and link its recorded call reference. Headers read "Output of t650: $ <command>" ("Output of t650" when the invocation is not loaded), the call reference linking to the call; the card\'s own block id stays alone at the right, one space after the status. No arrow glyphs mark call references. Successful completion output starts collapsed; nonzero exits and unknown outcomes stay open. Recorded exit status is right aligned with result metadata, including exit 0 on background completion cards. An attached result shows its recorded timestamp beside its first output line, not a blank header; omit it when its displayed timestamp matches the invocation. Preserve complete literal output, source references, history/provider data, and deterministic replay/reconnect. Restore the invariant that background output is tool output rather than an inter-session message. Use shared card chrome and disclosure behavior from task gwr. This replaces background completion wording from task 778 and the background-notice default from hyt; terminal and web both change as approved by the user.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Background completion cards keep their original transcript items and keys; web rows and terminal Look resolve the recorded call reference to its stored command when available. Missing/legacy invocations retain a literal Bash-output fallback and source link. Success is recognized only by a recorded exit 0; unknown outcomes stay open so errors are not silently hidden. Shared CardHeader inline chrome puts a delayed result timestamp and status beside the first output line. Compare displayed times to avoid repeated HH:MM stamps. Native CSS handles wrapping; there are no new timers or persistent indexes. A simple command already visible in a Bash title is not repeated in the web body, matching terminal behavior; custom presentations retain their raw command. Focused checks: 59 normal tests and 20 web-view tests passed; typecheck and changed-file lint passed. Chromium verified result color/source links, actual command titles, collapse/selection, header restoration, and an explicit two-minute result gap at 320 and 1200px. One-off geometry check was removed after passing; terminal scratch check covered same/missing/delayed timestamps and width limits. All-kind sticky matrix passed before a subsequent run failed during concurrent scroll work; agent 176-psi is investigating in task 981. No history/provider records or output bytes were changed.',
		"Call references dropped their arrow glyph (the user: arrows make no sense). Background output keeps the s letter from task 9p by the user's decision. A result shown apart from its call shows the bare call id (t1813) at the right: tool results have no block id of their own, so it is unambiguous."
